00:30:30.094 --> 00:30:31.728
Kiyoshi also has it,


00:30:31.761 --> 00:30:33.797
but it's yet to be
officially recognised.


00:30:33.831 --> 00:30:35.367
Alright? Got it?


00:30:36.601 --> 00:30:38.737
- Thank you.
- For sure.


00:30:45.308 --> 00:30:48.145
It's in my hands
and in... in my vision.


00:30:48.912 --> 00:30:52.883
But it's my son and those
like him that keep me going.


00:30:52.917 --> 00:30:54.452
Keep me fighting, you know.


00:30:54.485 --> 00:30:58.823
Sure. Does it ever affect
your ability to shoot?


00:30:58.855 --> 00:30:59.824
Oh.


00:30:59.856 --> 00:31:03.460
I may waste a little more film
than I should.


00:31:03.494 --> 00:31:07.398
But, for some reason,
with the camera, I'm not so bad.


00:31:07.430 --> 00:31:11.469
What, uh...
What's your endgame in this?


00:31:12.303 --> 00:31:14.805
Chisso
doesn't believe us patients.


00:31:14.838 --> 00:31:17.608
They don't believe
we are suffering.


00:31:17.642 --> 00:31:21.211
So we want to look
the president in the eyes.


00:31:21.245 --> 00:31:25.650
We want him to see us and then
tell us that we don't suffer.


00:31:26.450 --> 00:31:28.819
What makes you think
he's gonna listen to you?


00:31:28.853 --> 00:31:30.822
I don't know.


00:31:30.854 --> 00:31:33.458
Maybe if we make a noise
loud enough,


00:31:33.490 --> 00:31:35.459
they won't have a choice.


00:31:36.259 --> 00:31:39.396
With you,
we have a better chance.


00:34:49.853 --> 00:34:52.089
I hate that shit.


00:34:57.060 --> 00:34:59.564
I used to fucking hate
gym class.


00:34:59.596 --> 00:35:02.999
They used to make us all
sit down in a row,


00:35:03.033 --> 00:35:06.171
cross-legged, you know?


00:35:06.971 --> 00:35:10.341
And I couldn't do it. My legs
just don't work like that.


00:35:10.373 --> 00:35:12.576
They don't work
like that.


00:35:14.245 --> 00:35:16.346
And...


00:35:21.685 --> 00:35:24.422
I know you don't understand
a word that I'm saying,


00:35:24.455 --> 00:35:28.026
but that's not gonna stop me
from talking, so...


00:35:30.527 --> 00:35:33.797
..you might as well
just dig in, kid.


00:35:34.832 --> 00:35:36.500
You like jazz?


00:35:39.937 --> 00:35:45.109
Well, you'd better, 'cause
jazz... jazz is what we've got.


00:35:45.142 --> 00:35:48.846
It's just fucking jazz.


00:35:50.147 --> 00:35:53.116
Improvisation. Everything.


00:35:53.149 --> 00:35:54.184
See this?


00:35:55.518 --> 00:35:58.089
Anyone could do this. Anyone.


00:35:58.122 --> 00:35:59.757
Takes nothing.


00:36:00.558 --> 00:36:04.696
You point, focus, click.


00:36:06.096 --> 00:36:08.733
And most important... fuck up.


00:36:08.765 --> 00:36:13.337
Fuck up because that's
the only way to learn.


00:36:14.138 --> 00:36:16.239
So...


00:36:16.272 --> 00:36:17.975
..you take it, kid.


00:36:18.007 --> 00:36:19.676
I'm sick of it.


00:36:20.643 --> 00:36:24.415
I should have known better...
coming here.


00:36:25.281 --> 00:36:27.117
So you go on.


00:36:27.151 --> 00:36:29.087
Play the music.


00:36:34.058 --> 00:36:35.527
I'm, uh...


00:36:36.493 --> 00:36:40.064
I'm not really sure if I can
hear it anymore, you know?


00:37:17.935 --> 00:37:19.437
I don't believe you.


00:37:19.469 --> 00:37:21.339
I mean, what kind of
photographer


00:37:21.372 --> 00:37:23.007
gives the camera away?


00:37:23.040 --> 00:37:24.375
Unbelievable!


00:37:26.877 --> 00:37:30.547
Passing the torch, Aileen,
is how one dies gracefully.


00:37:30.580 --> 00:37:31.915
Somebody said that once.


00:37:31.948 --> 00:37:32.816
- You alright?
- What?


00:37:32.850 --> 00:37:34.886
Yeah, Kiyoshi.


00:37:35.752 --> 00:37:37.555
It's probably best
you know this now.


00:37:37.587 --> 00:37:41.158
I disappoint people
and I disappoint people always.


00:37:41.190 --> 00:37:42.727
Where are we?


00:37:42.759 --> 00:37:46.062
Ah, Aileen found you two
a little home to stay in.


00:37:46.096 --> 00:37:48.399
- What? Really?
- Yes.


00:37:48.431 --> 00:37:50.033
Me and her?


00:37:50.067 --> 00:37:51.469
Yes.


00:37:51.502 --> 00:37:53.137
Wow. That was nice.


00:37:53.169 --> 00:37:55.038
Come with me.


00:38:00.743 --> 00:38:04.348
We also put together
a darkroom for you.


00:38:10.921 --> 00:38:14.024
I set it up just the way
you have back home.


00:38:58.701 --> 00:39:00.171
Thank you.


00:39:00.203 --> 00:39:02.839
Pleasure.


00:39:08.178 --> 00:39:10.714
<i>Gene, good news.
We're moving up your piece.</i>


00:39:10.747 --> 00:39:12.782
<i>I think we might have an issue
with more photographs</i>


00:39:12.815 --> 00:39:14.984
<i>than car ads for the first time
for three years.</i>


00:39:15.018 --> 00:39:17.455
<i>It turns out there's
a UN environmental conference</i>


00:39:17.488 --> 00:39:18.922
<i>in Stockholm in a month.</i>


00:39:18.955 --> 00:39:21.858
<i>Very first of its kind.
We need to coordinate the two.</i>


00:39:21.892 --> 00:39:23.359
Gee whiz, Bob,


00:39:23.393 --> 00:39:25.463
I don't think I've heard you,
uh, this excited


00:39:25.495 --> 00:39:26.997
since they faked
the moon landing.


00:39:27.029 --> 00:39:30.301
<i>And Millie has shaken every
tree with the anti-nuke folks</i>


00:39:30.334 --> 00:39:32.937
and the WHO here and in Japan.


00:39:32.969 --> 00:39:35.105
We have all the science
to highlight your images.


00:39:35.138 --> 00:39:36.506
Is he saving
his receipts?


00:39:36.540 --> 00:39:38.275
So, how's it going out there?


00:39:38.308 --> 00:39:39.910
Oh, it's... it's fun. It's fun.


00:39:39.942 --> 00:39:42.178
I'm having a great time.
I wish you were here.


00:39:42.212 --> 00:39:43.881
I'd... I'd... I'd let you
buy me a drink.


00:39:43.913 --> 00:39:45.616
<i>There's no wiggle room
on this one, Gene.</i>


00:39:45.649 --> 00:39:48.719
<i>If we don't have the images
by next week, we won't make it.</i>


00:39:49.986 --> 00:39:51.387
You know what? What?!


00:39:51.421 --> 00:39:53.123
- <i>Gene...</i>
- I got a bad connection, Bob.


00:39:53.156 --> 00:39:54.825
- I've got a bad connection.
- <i>Gene...</i>


00:39:58.629 --> 00:40:01.531
Yeah, I might have had
a little something to drink


00:40:01.564 --> 00:40:03.900
and I didn't know
what I was doing.


00:40:18.181 --> 00:40:19.716
I asked the people to give


00:40:19.750 --> 00:40:22.620
whatever cameras
and film they had.


00:40:22.652 --> 00:40:24.187
Oh!


00:40:29.960 --> 00:40:33.130
Maybe you can join me
thanking the people.


00:40:33.163 --> 00:40:36.000
Oh, yeah. Thank you. Thanks.


00:40:36.033 --> 00:40:37.201
Bow.


00:40:37.234 --> 00:40:39.469
Alright.


00:40:40.636 --> 00:40:42.105
Thank you.


00:40:43.339 --> 00:40:45.042
Thank you.


00:40:47.143 --> 00:40:48.779
That's my camera.


00:40:49.712 --> 00:40:51.481
Yeah, that's me.
That's mine.


00:40:51.515 --> 00:40:53.785
Great. Got it. Alright.


00:40:54.585 --> 00:40:56.387
Well, that's alright.


00:41:01.158 --> 00:41:04.328
- What?
- How is it turn into photos?


00:41:06.495 --> 00:41:08.665
Then you turn it
like this. Alright?


00:41:08.698 --> 00:41:10.800
Turn it like this.
Come here, you do it.


00:41:10.834 --> 00:41:12.169
Give me your hands.


00:41:12.201 --> 00:41:14.571
Here. Take that. OK?


00:41:14.605 --> 00:41:15.506
Right?


00:41:15.540 --> 00:41:17.608
Put that hand there.
OK, now, I got you.


00:41:17.640 --> 00:41:21.044
Now, just turn it like that.
Right?


00:41:22.044 --> 00:41:25.882
Like that.


00:41:27.084 --> 00:41:29.319
You're not afraid to touch me?


00:41:31.788 --> 00:41:33.424
Why would I be?


00:41:40.062 --> 00:41:43.334
Your hands shake because
you have Minamata disease too?


00:41:43.366 --> 00:41:47.504
No, no. No, no. I...
No, I just drink a bunch.


00:41:47.536 --> 00:41:49.640
What's this kid's name?


00:41:49.672 --> 00:41:51.341
Sigeru!


00:41:51.375 --> 00:41:53.611
Ah. Now...


00:41:53.643 --> 00:41:55.346
Gene.


00:41:59.783 --> 00:42:03.853
Um... it's getting late.
Maybe he should be in bed, no?


00:42:03.886 --> 00:42:05.655
Thanks, kid.


00:42:15.265 --> 00:42:17.167
He wants to learn how to make


00:42:17.200 --> 00:42:18.835
the film strip
into big pictures.


00:42:18.868 --> 00:42:23.806
Um, I'm not really here
to give photography classes.


00:42:23.839 --> 00:42:27.510
Especially to kids.


00:42:30.247 --> 00:42:32.382
OK, I'll teach him.
I'll teach you.


00:42:33.183 --> 00:42:36.087
Um... you take it.


00:42:37.087 --> 00:42:38.489
Here. You got it?


00:42:38.522 --> 00:42:40.524
And you will take
some pictures, huh?


00:42:40.556 --> 00:42:42.792
And we'll develop them later.


00:42:44.428 --> 00:42:45.629
Hmm.


00:42:45.661 --> 00:42:46.462
OK?


00:42:49.933 --> 00:42:51.469
Arigato.


00:42:52.268 --> 00:42:53.837
OK, pal.


00:43:00.410 --> 00:43:02.279
- Pretty good, that kid.
- Mm-hm.


00:43:02.312 --> 00:43:04.714
- You like that one?
- Can I have it?


00:43:04.747 --> 00:43:07.016
No. You can't just have it. No.


00:43:07.049 --> 00:43:09.053
Maybe I can help?


00:43:10.219 --> 00:43:11.888
You know, uh...


00:43:13.290 --> 00:43:14.959
..the Native Americans,


00:43:14.991 --> 00:43:16.926
they believed that a photograph


00:43:16.960 --> 00:43:20.097
would take a piece
of the subject's soul.


00:43:20.129 --> 00:43:24.200
But what... what gets left out
of the fine print is...


00:43:25.002 --> 00:43:29.507
..that it can also take a piece
of the photographer's soul.


00:43:30.640 --> 00:43:33.444
You understand what I'm saying?
It, uh...


00:43:34.477 --> 00:43:36.413
It will break your heart.


00:43:37.547 --> 00:43:39.717
So, if you take it...


00:43:40.917 --> 00:43:42.853
..you take it seriously.


00:43:43.853 --> 00:43:45.823
Agreed?


00:44:03.372 --> 00:44:05.041
- Put your stuff here.
- Mmm.


00:44:16.319 --> 00:44:17.922
Goddamn.


00:44:19.489 --> 00:44:22.059
Phew.
I'm glad that worked.


00:44:49.953 --> 00:44:51.488
May I? May I?


00:44:51.520 --> 00:44:53.423
Yes.


00:45:20.917 --> 00:45:23.953
OK, I'm gonna see if I can
find something we can use


00:45:23.986 --> 00:45:25.789
at the shareholders meeting.


00:45:42.906 --> 00:45:47.911
It's OK to take a picture.
Just don't show his face.


00:45:47.944 --> 00:45:49.346
Right. Hey, listen.


00:45:49.379 --> 00:45:52.049
People must see what's going on
behind the eyes


00:45:52.082 --> 00:45:54.218
because that's where
the truth is.


00:45:54.250 --> 00:45:55.651
It's an empathy thing.


00:45:55.685 --> 00:45:58.522
- I need faces.
- Well, we need empathy here.


00:46:02.625 --> 00:46:03.893
OK.


00:46:26.382 --> 00:46:28.352
Thank you, sir.


00:46:29.152 --> 00:46:30.988
Arigato.


00:47:07.056 --> 00:47:09.426
OK. Let's go find the nursery.


00:47:14.598 --> 00:47:16.866
Oh. That's... Yeah.


00:47:16.899 --> 00:47:18.334
Uh, let's turn around now.


00:47:18.368 --> 00:47:20.036
- Let's go.
- Go this way.


00:47:23.306 --> 00:47:25.509
Just keep going.
Just keep going.


00:47:26.776 --> 00:47:29.078
Slip in here. Quick,
quick, quick, quick, quick.


00:47:33.283 --> 00:47:36.053
Gene! Aileen!
I found the lab.


00:47:37.120 --> 00:47:39.756
Dr Yamashita's been
the chief doctor for Chisso


00:47:39.788 --> 00:47:42.359
since the first victims
showed up.


00:47:42.392 --> 00:47:44.127
They had to be running tests.


00:47:44.160 --> 00:47:45.928
They must have found something.


00:48:44.421 --> 00:48:46.589
Hey! I found something.


00:48:51.627 --> 00:48:55.298
It says the cat he fed
from Chisso's pipe water


00:48:55.332 --> 00:48:57.768
reacted just like the patients.


00:48:58.935 --> 00:49:00.203
Spasms.


00:49:00.236 --> 00:49:02.172
Paralysis.


00:49:02.205 --> 00:49:04.375
Convulsions.


00:49:05.241 --> 00:49:07.511
Which is exactly what happened


00:49:07.544 --> 00:49:09.980
when one is poisoned
with mercury.


00:49:10.747 --> 00:49:14.084
It literally destroys
brain tissue.


00:49:15.151 --> 00:49:18.455
And for 15 years, they knew.


00:49:19.254 --> 00:49:20.723
They knew, Gene.


00:49:20.756 --> 00:49:23.292
And they kept poisoning people.


00:49:23.326 --> 00:49:25.062
Give me that.


00:49:25.094 --> 00:49:29.767
You turn around, pick up your
camera, check your settings.


00:49:30.567 --> 00:49:34.571
You cannot let your emotions
run the show


00:49:34.603 --> 00:49:36.540
'cause you will fucking lose


00:49:36.573 --> 00:49:39.743
and sometimes
you might fucking die.


00:49:39.776 --> 00:49:42.645
Focus on the photograph
you want to take.


00:49:42.678 --> 00:49:46.615
Focus on what you want to say.


00:49:46.649 --> 00:49:48.417
Do it now.


00:49:58.093 --> 00:50:01.230
You remember how it
affected you emotionally, right?


00:50:01.263 --> 00:50:03.099
How did it make you feel?


00:50:03.132 --> 00:50:05.067
Was it unpleasant?


00:50:05.100 --> 00:50:07.770
A... a menace? Was it evil?


00:50:09.506 --> 00:50:11.942
Just over here. You're changing.


00:50:13.109 --> 00:50:14.411
Many things.


00:50:14.444 --> 00:50:16.246
Yeah. OK.


00:50:16.279 --> 00:50:17.614
Now...


00:50:18.814 --> 00:50:20.350
Take it out.


00:50:22.051 --> 00:50:23.620
Dump it in the soup.


00:50:26.189 --> 00:50:28.257
So here's a little secret
of mine.


00:50:28.290 --> 00:50:30.326
Use your hands a lot.


00:50:30.359 --> 00:50:32.062
Caress the image.


00:50:32.094 --> 00:50:34.263
You warm the print


00:50:34.297 --> 00:50:38.001
with the body heat
from your hands.


00:50:38.033 --> 00:50:40.803
That's how you tell your story.


00:50:45.207 --> 00:50:47.043
OK.


00:50:49.111 --> 00:50:51.948
Now, here. Dry your hands.


00:50:55.350 --> 00:50:57.353
Thank you.


00:50:57.386 --> 00:50:59.089
What for?


00:51:00.689 --> 00:51:02.392
Oh, wait.


00:51:03.192 --> 00:51:05.461
Ooh. Don't move.
Don't move. Don't move.


00:51:09.399 --> 00:51:11.667
Click.


00:51:12.468 --> 00:51:15.805
Aren't you supposed to ask
permission first?


00:51:15.839 --> 00:51:18.607
Permission... permission is like
asking for a kiss, no.


00:51:18.640 --> 00:51:21.644
It destroys the moment.
You just gotta take it.


00:51:26.049 --> 00:51:27.684
Like that?


00:51:28.484 --> 00:51:31.020
Something like that, yes. Yeah.


00:51:35.792 --> 00:51:37.326
Just, uh...


00:51:37.359 --> 00:51:41.064
..try not to forget
about the fine print, kid.


00:51:42.698 --> 00:51:44.401
Hmm.


00:52:36.919 --> 00:52:38.687
No, no!


00:52:38.721 --> 00:52:40.489
Gene!


00:52:42.158 --> 00:52:43.794
It's OK.


00:52:44.794 --> 00:52:46.062
I'll be back.


00:53:05.348 --> 00:53:08.352
Mr Smith. Come in.


00:53:09.451 --> 00:53:11.555
- Thank you.
- Please sit.


00:53:14.156 --> 00:53:16.292
Would you like something
to drink? Water?


00:53:16.326 --> 00:53:18.094
You know, I actually think
I'd rather wait


00:53:18.127 --> 00:53:20.363
until I get outside the building
before I drop dead,


00:53:20.395 --> 00:53:23.767
so, um, perhaps a soda pop,
you know,


00:53:23.799 --> 00:53:27.169
with the top still on it,
in the bottle.


00:53:27.203 --> 00:53:28.605
OK.


00:53:38.881 --> 00:53:40.517
Thank you.


00:53:41.417 --> 00:53:46.989
Mr Smith, do you know what
'parts per million' means?


00:53:47.924 --> 00:53:50.994
Without getting confused
by all the science,


00:53:51.027 --> 00:53:54.698
it is a very, very small amount.


00:53:54.730 --> 00:53:58.734
And small amounts are accepted.


00:53:59.736 --> 00:54:04.308
Even in this bottle,
unopened bottle of cola...


00:54:05.107 --> 00:54:10.580
..there may be the tiniest
amount of some material


00:54:10.613 --> 00:54:14.484
you might not expect
or appreciate.


00:54:14.517 --> 00:54:19.522
But it's microscopic.
Barely even there.


00:54:21.357 --> 00:54:23.226
May I show you something?


00:54:23.259 --> 00:54:24.895
Look over there.


00:54:28.931 --> 00:54:30.534
The Cyclator.


00:54:32.502 --> 00:54:34.504
We spent much money
creating a system


00:54:34.536 --> 00:54:36.906
that keeps the water safe.


00:54:36.939 --> 00:54:42.779
Huh. I even drank from it
to prove its safety.


00:54:50.453 --> 00:54:52.555
It's... it's a great photograph.


00:54:52.587 --> 00:54:54.189
It's really a nice photograph.


00:54:54.223 --> 00:54:56.493
- Oh, thank you.
- You're welcome.


00:54:59.594 --> 00:55:02.866
So... let's take a walk.


00:55:05.201 --> 00:55:07.738
Do you know what we make here?


00:55:08.738 --> 00:55:10.239
Toxic chemicals.


00:55:10.272 --> 00:55:12.408
Good chemicals.


00:55:15.377 --> 00:55:19.548
Chemicals that have
fertilised the land.


00:55:20.315 --> 00:55:22.651
Help feed millions.


00:55:22.685 --> 00:55:28.091
And chemicals needed to make
plastics, even medicines.


00:55:28.890 --> 00:55:33.395
Also chemicals
for developing photographs.


00:55:33.428 --> 00:55:38.434
And chemicals
that make 35mm film.


00:55:39.234 --> 00:55:42.805
Like the kind you use yourself,
Mr Smith.


00:55:43.605 --> 00:55:47.910
We employ over 60%
of the residents here.


00:55:47.944 --> 00:55:50.714
If the protesters succeed,


00:55:50.747 --> 00:55:54.017
and they put Chisso
out of business,


00:55:54.049 --> 00:55:56.553
what happens then?


00:55:56.585 --> 00:55:58.821
I mean,
how the fuck would I know?


00:56:01.690 --> 00:56:05.728
I know that you are broke,
Mr Smith.


00:56:07.096 --> 00:56:08.998
That you owe money


00:56:09.031 --> 00:56:13.570
and that you are on brink
of getting evicted.


00:56:13.602 --> 00:56:15.938
You are correct, sir.


00:56:15.971 --> 00:56:17.439
You are very correct.


00:56:17.473 --> 00:56:20.143
But I've still got my youth...


00:56:21.009 --> 00:56:24.413
..and my girly charm, which
I think will get me through.


00:56:26.015 --> 00:56:31.955
A father is supposed to provide
and protect his children.


00:56:32.754 --> 00:56:36.593
Obviously, you care
more about yourself


00:56:36.625 --> 00:56:39.428
than your own flesh and blood.


00:56:44.466 --> 00:56:48.103
Now, you may choose to believe


00:56:48.136 --> 00:56:50.739
the small amount
of the local fishermen


00:56:50.772 --> 00:56:56.845
who claim that
they have somehow been harmed


00:56:56.879 --> 00:56:59.015
by our methods.


